---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { BRAND } from "@vc/config";
import { isMarketingHost } from "../../server/public-blog";
import { publicRuntimeEnv } from "../../server/runtime";

const env = publicRuntimeEnv(Astro);
if (env.selfHosted || !isMarketingHost(Astro.request, env)) {
  return new Response("Not found", {
    status: 404,
    headers: { "content-type": "text/plain; charset=utf-8" },
  });
}
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Support"
  description={`How to get help with ${BRAND.name}.`}
  updated="August 16, 2026"
>
  <h2>Bug reports and feature ideas</h2>
  <p>
    vibecms is open source. The fastest route for bugs, regressions, and feature ideas is a
    GitHub issue, which gets a tracked, public answer:{" "}
    <a href={BRAND.repoUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">{BRAND.repoUrl.replace("https://", "")}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Account, billing, and private matters</h2>
  <p>
    Anything involving your workspace, invoices, tokens, or content privacy goes to{" "}
    <a href="mailto:support@vibecms.dev">support@vibecms.dev</a> from the email you sign in with.
    Tell us the symptom and what you expected instead; posting your token is never necessary and
    please do not include it.
  </p>

  <h2>Response time and status</h2>
  <p>
    During public early access, support is best-effort: we aim to answer within two business
    days, usually much faster. There is no live chat or public status page yet. When a broad
    incident occurs, we will post an update on the site and GitHub.
  </p>

  <h2>What helps us help you</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your blog URL and the email on the workspace.</li>
    <li>What you did, what happened, and what you expected.</li>
    <li>For agent or MCP issues: the client and version, and the action that failed.</li>
  </ul>
</LegalLayout>
